"edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-2/trig-omp-reported/1/workspace", "first_after_build": true, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`test_dates` passes now. In `dates/parse.py`, `parse_date` calls `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime` with `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"`. That format had nothing to match the trailing `Z`, which caused the error. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass.\n\nWhat changes for callers:\n- Timestamps ending in `Z` or an offset like `+02:00` now come back timezone-aware: `...Z` gives `tzinfo=timezone.utc`, and `+02:00` gives a UTC+2 offset.\n- Timestamps with no zone still come back without a timezone, as before, so `test_naive` and `day_key` behave the same.\n- It also accepts other ISO-8601 forms the old format rejected, such as fractional seconds or a bare date.\n- If any code compares these results with datetimes that have no timezone, Python raises a `TypeError`. Inside this repo the only caller is `day_key`, which isn't affected.\n- This needs Python 3.11 or later; older `fromisoformat` doesn't accept `Z`. The repo doesn't pin a version, and this machine runs 3.13.5.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok